    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Moovingo Estate Agents are delighted to present 255 Swords Road to the market. This is an attractive 1950s semi-detached property. This house will appeal to anyone who is looking for a stylish, large, extended family home near the city.\r\n\r\nIt has been tastefully decorated and designed and has an uplifting atmosphere in which a wonderful sense of space and light prevails. The house blends a sense of old world charm with modern day living and it\r\nhas every convenience at its doorstep.\r\n\r\nIt consists of hallway; cloakroom and under stairs storage space; kitchen/dining-room; sitting-room; 4 bedroomed accommodation (the converted garage room is currently used as a bedroom but could be\r\nan office, playroom etc); magnificent sunroom/family room; two bathrooms (one downstairs with power shower and one upstairs with bath).\r\n\r\nThe impressive sunroom//family room overlooks the beautiful, mature, landscaped back garden which includes a Japanese cherry tree and a gorgeous philadelphus plant (mock orange blossom tree) as well as several other varieties of trees and plants/shrubs.\r\n\r\nThe garden is an oasis of nature teeming with birdsong and leafy nooks for relaxation and yet the location is only 25 minutes from O’Connell St. and 7 minutes to Dublin Airport (5 minutes to the M1 and M50). At the end of the rear garden there is access to a private laneway for vehicular deliveries.\r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION\r\n\r\nDOWNSTAIRS:\r\nEntrance Hall:\r\nSolid wooden floor, coved ceiling, dado rail , cloakroom with under stairs storage, landline and broadband connection points.\r\n\r\nLiving Room:\r\n4.10m x 3.85m. Solid wooden floor, feature tiled fireplace with gas fire insert, coved ceiling, bay window and sliding double doors.\r\n\r\nDining Room:\r\n3.80m. x 3.40m. Solid wooden floor, feature tiled fireplace, coved ceiling and double doors leading to kitchen.\r\n\r\nKitchen:\r\n5.20m. x 4.20m. L shaped room with tiled floor, wall and floor mounted units, plumbed for dishwasher and washing machines, 13 electrical power points, landline phone point, double doors leading to south-west facing rear garden.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1(Downstairs/Converted Garage):\r\n4.95m. x 2.60m. Semi-solid American walnut wooden floor, feature Spanish marble fireplace with fan assisted gas fire insert, landline phone point, dado rail, coved ceiling and two ‘niches’ or arched recesses as features.\r\n\r\nSunRoom/Family Room:\r\n4.85m. x 2.95m. Semi-solid oak wooden floor, spot lights recessed in ceiling, 4x Velux windows, double doors leading to S.W. facing garden.\r\n\r\nDownstairs Bathroom:\r\n2.40m. x 1.50m. Tiled walls and floor in Travertine stone, WC, WHB,, power shower with seat, extractor fan.\r\n\r\nUPSTAIRS:\r\n\r\nBedroom 2:\r\n4.30m. x 3.40m. Solid wooden floor, bay window, 3 feature light fittings on side walls.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3:\r\n3.40m. x 3.80m. Solid wooden floor.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4/ Box Room:\r\n2.55m. x 2. 85m. Solid wooden floor, feature spotlight on side wall, broadband/phone point.\r\n\r\nBathroom:\r\nFully tiled floor & walls, bath,WHB, hot press. (Separate room for WC)\r\n\r\nLanding:\r\nSolid wooden floor & access to attic\r\n\r\nGarden\r\nFront- driveway + mature planting and rockery in garden.\r\nBack- long back garden south-west facing-22.15m. or 72.5 ft., landscaped with select array of plants, shrubs, and mature trees.\r\n\r\nArea Info:\r\n\r\nThe area is well served by amenities within walking distance e.g. two parks Ellenfield (within 5 mins.’walking distance ) and Santry Demesne (15 mins) Omni Park Shopping Centre (5 mins.); Beaumont Hospital (15 mins.); Dublin City University (12mins.) The location is particularly well served with public transport by bus & taxi e.g. Bus nos. 41/41C/33/16/1 (and the 104 to Clontarf & DCU via Santry).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: Any intending purchaser(s) shall accept that no statement, description or measurement contained in advertisement or any other document or published by the vendor or by Moovingo, in respect of the premises shall constitute a representation inducing the purchaser(s) to enter into any contract for sale, or any warranty forming part of any such contract for sale. Any such statement, description or measurement, whether in writing or in oral form, given by the vendor, or by Moovingo, are for illustration purposes only and are not to be taken as matters of fact. Any intending purchaser(s) shall satisfy themselves by inspection, survey or otherwise as to the correctness of same. No omission, misstatement, misdescription, incorrect measurement or error of any description, whether given orally or in any written form by the vendor or by Moovingo, shall give rise to any claim for compensation against the vendor or against Moovingo. Any intending purchaser(s) are deemed to fully satisfy themselves in relation to all such matters."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Sun room / family room extension\r\nConverted garage / downstairs bedroom with marble fireplace & two ‘niches’ or arched recesses as features.\r\nMature landscaped gardens & South-West facing back garden.\r\nRear access to private laneway\r\n4 Security lights (3 at back & 1 at front of house)\r\nKitchen has 13 electrical power points\r\n7 mins. to Dublin Airport, 5 mins. to M50 & M1\r\n25 mins. to city centre\r\nVery well serviced transport links(24 hrs.) with choice of buses- nos. 41/41B/41C/33/16/1 & 104\r\nVery close to Omni Park Shopping Centre & IMC Cinemas, schools, shops and businesses on the doorstep\r\n12 mins.’ walk to D.C.U.\r\nPolished, real wooden floors throughout (exception of tiled kitchen & bathroom floors)\r\nClose to parks : Ellenfield Park (5 mins.’ walk) & Santry Demesne (15 mins’ walk)"
